Hi Martin,

This looks fine to me. M2 is computing a measure of lack-of-fit, so seeing RMSEA ≈ 0 is likely given the smaller sample size information. All you would say in this case is there is no evidence for lack of fit in light of the fitted models and observed data. HTH.

Phil

